WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.617
Correlation measures the strength and direction of a linear relationship between two numeric variables.

00:00:07.617 --> 00:00:14.512
Here hours studied increases as score increases, so we expect a strong positive correlation.

00:00:14.512 --> 00:00:20.025
A value close to one indicates a strong positive linear relationship.

00:00:20.475 --> 00:00:23.377
But correlation does not prove causation.

00:00:23.377 --> 00:00:30.357
Two variables can move together because of other factors, reverse direction, or coincidence.

00:00:30.357 --> 00:00:37.090
Use correlation as evidence of association, not as proof that one variable causes the other.
